  "readmeFile": "docs\\README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.1.0 — Secure-by-default TLS + optional relax toggles\n\n• TLS validation is now strict by default. The SDK overrides RabbitMQ.Client's lenient URI default\n  (which pre-flags RemoteCertificateNameMismatch as acceptable) and rejects connections where the\n  server certificate's Subject/SAN does not match the URI host or where the chain cannot be built\n  to a trusted root.\n\n• New optional parameter on CreateSdkAsync:\n  CreateSdkAsync(connectionString, exchange, BusSslOptions? sslOptions = null)\n  Existing 2-arg callers are unchanged at the source level; they now get strict TLS at runtime.\n\n• New BusSslOptions record with opt-in flags for legitimate non-strict cases:\n  - AllowHostnameMismatch — accept certs whose SAN does not match the URI host\n    (e.g. IP-based connections, aliased hostnames).\n  - AllowUntrustedChain   — accept certs whose chain cannot be built to a trusted root\n    (e.g. self-signed dev certs).\n  Defaults for both: false (strict).\n\n• MessagePack bumped 3.1.4 → 3.1.6.\n\nNote for upgraders: any connection that previously succeeded only because of the lenient name-check\ndefault will now fail with a TLS validation error. Either fix the cert SAN / URI host so they match,\nor pass BusSslOptions with the matching flag set.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": false,
  "verbatimVersion": "2.1.0",
